WEBVTT

00:10:29.457 --> 00:10:32.411
I think they use interactions to assess density,

00:10:32.411 --> 00:10:33.640
so when they're really crowded,

00:10:33.640 --> 00:10:34.742
they meet more often,

00:10:34.742 --> 00:10:37.207
and they search more thoroughly.

00:10:37.207 --> 00:10:40.607
Different ant species must use different algorithms,

00:10:40.607 --> 00:10:43.129
because they've evolved to deal with

00:10:43.129 --> 00:10:44.800
different resources,

00:10:44.800 --> 00:10:47.359
and it could be really useful to know about this,

00:10:47.359 --> 00:10:49.001
and so we recently asked ants

00:10:49.001 --> 00:10:51.451
to solve the collective search problem

00:10:51.451 --> 00:10:52.819
in the extreme environment

00:10:52.819 --> 00:10:54.377
of microgravity

00:10:54.377 --> 00:10:56.353
in the International Space Station.

00:10:56.353 --> 00:10:57.898
When I first saw this picture, I thought,

00:10:57.898 --> 00:11:00.755
Oh no, they've mounted the habitat vertically,